  "limitations": [
    "Balanced target-category positives/negative controls selected by author human labels, therefore a per-study enriched test and no deployment prevalence; reported precision does not transfer to real GUIs",
    "Human source has_strong_agreement is the released dataset flag, not a guaranteed unanimous three-annotator adjudication; only 20 strong low-contrast positives",
    "Some source images are deliberately altered slide images, real authored origins mixed; category-negative slides may exhibit other mistakes",
    "Low color-contrast inferred by grayscale pixel quantiles inside OCR word boxes is NOT proper foreground/background WCAG computed contrast and can mislabel photos/gradients",
    "Clipping inside widget containers is not equivalent to text touching physical slide boundary; occluded shapes may not appear as two OCR word boxes",
    "Generic CLIP prompt softmax is uncalibrated; no semantic visual judgment, cannot locate faults or certify layout",
    "Source-trained 16-feature classifier used category human labels for fitting and tested leave-one-slide-source-type-out; not a pretrained image model or independent untouched deployment set",
    "Operational OCR timeouts are ABSTAINS, not genuine negative judgments. Report complete paired coverage alongside conservative default-negative counts",
    "Bounding box localization against human broad regions requires random chance-area comparison; high center hit can be trivial if gold region covers much of slide",
    "No guarantee of actual application GUI performance; narrow companion to real Firefox ScreenParser and W3C axe-core benchmarks already committed"
  ]
}
